      "location": "Proof 2.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The proof says, “A map with contractible fibres is a weak homotopy equivalence,” then extends this to the formal restriction map by analogy. Contractible fibres alone do not imply weak homotopy equivalence, and the item establishes no homotopy-lifting property for these restriction maps. The stated shrink along disk fibres also changes the vertical derivative at the zero section by the shrink factor, so it does not contract the fibre with its prescribed normal-bundle identification fixed; at factor zero it loses injectivity. The formal restriction claim therefore lacks a licensed argument.",
