      "id": "lem-smoothing-formal-immersion-families",
      "location": "Proof 1.2, 2.1 and 3.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Historical defect in the exact observed pre-reader bytes. The concurrently revised current supplier now addresses the listed objections; this finding does not claim those defects persist in the revision. Proof 1.2 says restriction of the adjoint bundle map to the zero section yields its Hom-bundle coefficients, but that restriction gives only the zero vector over f(p,x), losing F; coefficients must be recovered by evaluating a local frame. More seriously, 2.1 applies unrestricted manifold-valued Whitney approximation to sigma(p,x)=(x,f(p,x),F(p,x)) in the total Hom bundle over M x N. Its approximation and ambient retraction need not preserve the M-coordinate x. Step 3.1 then interprets the resulting linear map on T_(x_s)M as a map on T_xM, without an identification or base-preserving approximation. The cited relative Whitney theorem only supplies a manifold-valued approximation. A section-preserving parametric approximation (or explicit base correction and tangent transport), with joint jet continuity and injectivity control, is needed.",
